    how: { eyebrow: 'How it works', title: 'From loose information to history that helps decisions.', lead: 'The guided cycle shortens the path between understanding and acting without taking control away from the person doing the work.', cycle: [['Capture', 'Text, photos, documents and operational information enter the flow.'], ['Understand', 'Content gains structure and context inside the business.'], ['Confirm', 'The user reviews and remains in control of important operations.'], ['Register', 'Information becomes useful, traceable history.'], ['Follow up', 'Rumman brings back what needs attention and context.']] },
    plans: { eyebrow: 'Plans', title: 'Choose the room your operation needs.', lead: 'Launch plans for small businesses, with Premium trial access and transparent limits.', essential: 'Essential', pro: 'Pro', team: 'Team', monthly: '/month', annualOne: 'or R$ 499 per year', annualTwo: 'or R$ 899 per year', annualThree: 'or R$ 1,499 per year', featured: 'More capacity', trial: '15 days of Premium trial.', trialText: 'The trial requires Google Play subscription activation. After the period, the selected plan is billed unless cancelled.', limitText: 'There is no permanent free tier, unlimited AI or unlimited storage.' },
    faq: { eyebrow: 'Frequently asked questions', title: 'What to know before getting started.', lead: 'Clear answers about the product, data, intelligence, inventory and availability.', sideEyebrow: 'Rumman', sideTitle: 'Clarity is part of the product.', items: [['Is Rumman an ERP?', 'Yes. It is a guided ERP for micro and small businesses, bringing together customers, finance, operations, inventory, purchasing, documents and operational assistance.'], ['Does everything stay in the cloud?', 'No. Detailed data stays primarily on the device. Rumman cloud services are limited to account, protection, summary, diagnostics, subscription and requested AI. Separately, when device backup is enabled, Android may store the operational database in the user’s private Google Account backup area.'], ['What happens if I lose or replace my phone?', 'With device backup enabled, Android may restore the Rumman operational database using the same Google Account. Android controls this feature, which has a total limit of 25 MB per app and usually runs once a day when system conditions are met. Credentials, tokens, cache, scanned images and attachments are excluded.'], ['Does Rumman sell my data or show ads?', 'No. Rumman does not sell data and does not show ads.'], ['Does AI make financial decisions by itself?', 'No. It is designed to organize and guide. Important operations remain under the user confirmation and control.'], ['Is it already available on Google Play?', 'There is no public listing yet. The product is being prepared for closed testing.'], ['Does Rumman manage inventory?', 'Yes. The workflow records inbound and outbound movements, separates physical, reserved and available stock, and guides replenishment.']] },
